    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0270" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg190"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Count von Quadt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 565.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 30th ultimo, informing me of the dates on which his
                    majesty’s schoolships <hi rendition="#italic">Moltke</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stein</hi> will visit certain cities of the United
                    States, Porto Rico, and Cuba.</p>
                <p>With a view to the extension of the usual courtesies to these vessels, I have
                    made the matter known to the heads of the Treasury, War, and Navy Departments
                    and to the governors of Maryland and Porto Rico.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
